mpleted":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I think there is a problem when using shadowmaps in combination with meshes that have doublesided set to true.\n\nplease see jsfiddle which illustrates the problem\nhttp://jsfiddle.net/pwerslv/xMSXf/2/\n\n(this is the shadowmap scene from the examples, with additional button that sets all meshes doublesided to true)\n\n1) run. all god.\n2) toggle doublesided button\n-> everything gets slightly darker. (not so bad)\n-> some areas seem to be fully shadowed (top area of three.js letters)\n\n![singlesided](http://s17.postimage.org/lj8hib4gr/shdscene_singlesided.png)\n[singlesided ](http://postimage.org/image/lj8hib4gr/)\n\n![doublesided](http://s17.postimage.org/fh0urtg0r/shdscene_doublesided.png)\n[doublesided ](http://postimage.org/image/fh0urtg0r/)\n\n---\n\nBelow are some images of a different scene. It seems that the completely shadowed areas are appearing on the area where the upper half of the shadow map is projected. again, this only happens on meshes with doublesided = true.\n\n![b1](http://s17.postimage.org/x38pwlo4b/shdmapbug01.png)\n[ b1](http://postimage.org/image/x38pwlo4b/)\n\n![b2](http://s17.postimage.org/r3kysy3bv/shdmapbug02.png)\n[ b2](http://postimage.org/image/r3kysy3bv/)\n\n![b3](http://s17.postimage.org/nl8ywk2fv/shdmapbug03.png)\n[ b3](http://postimage.org/image/nl8ywk2fv/)\n\nany ideas on that?\n","closed_by":{"login":"mrdoob","id":97088,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3MDg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97088?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob","html_url":"https://github.com/mrdoob","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/starred{/owner}{/repo}","